---
import WorkLayout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Thatpam from '../../components/sketches/Thatpam.astro';

const description = 'தட்பம் (Thatpam): a solo ed-tech experiment by Mariappan Subramanian — teaching frontend in Tamil, in tiny cohorts, and learning the business of teaching by running all of it alone, from pixels to payments.';
---
<WorkLayout
  title="தட்பம் (Thatpam)"
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Indie · Solo ed-tech experiment · 2021"
  heading="தட்பம்"
  headingLang="ta"
  facts={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Founder · teacher · designer · engineer' },
    { label: 'Cohorts', value: 'Small by design (~10 learners)' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'Paused, not closed' },
  ]}
  link={{ href: 'https://thatpam.netlify.app/', label: 'thatpam.netlify.app' }}
  schema={{
    name: 'தட்பம் (Thatpam)',
    alternateName: 'Thatpam',
    url: 'https://thatpam.netlify.app/',
    description: 'A solo ed-tech experiment to teach frontend in Tamil, in tiny cohorts, and to learn the business of teaching by running all of it alone — from pixels to payments.',
    inLanguage: ['ta', 'en'],
    keywords: 'ed-tech, Tamil, frontend, teaching, indie, solo founder',
  }}
>
  <Thatpam slot="sketch" />

  <Fragment slot="lede"><span lang="ta">திறமைக்கு மொழி தடை இல்லை</span> — talent has no language barrier. A solo experiment to teach frontend in Tamil, in tiny cohorts, and to learn the business of teaching by doing all of it myself — <mark class="hl">pixels to payments</mark>.</Fragment>

  <h2>The name</h2>
  <p><span lang="ta">தட்பம்</span> (<em>thatpam</em>) means coolness — a cool, breezy climate. I wanted learning to feel exactly like that: fresh, light, a little fun.</p>

  <h2>Why it existed</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>Job-switchers kept hitting the same wall: course syllabi that were generic and already out of date — college, repackaged.</li>
    <li>I was already teaching on other platforms and it never quite satisfied me. The real gap was current, in-trend frontend from someone who ships it daily.</li>
    <li>So when a couple of people asked for my time, I turned it into a thing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The bet: stay small on purpose</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>I kept cohorts deliberately tiny. No plan to grow the student base, hire tutors, or franchise it.</li>
    <li>The USP <em>was</em> the focus — a few serious people, my full attention, one goal: help them win their switch.</li>
    <li>It was never really about revenue. It was passion, and a taste of running something end to end.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Marketing, my way</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>No brand, no ad spend, no funnel. Just word of mouth and trust I'd earned — free guidance, YouTube lessons, hours spent with people before any money changed hands.</li>
    <li>Only once that trust existed did I put up a site and switch on payments.</li>
    <li>The lesson that stuck: find your own strength and write your own playbook; there's no fixed one.</li>
  </ul>

  <blockquote>I was the product — so I never needed a funnel.</blockquote>

  <h2>Where they are now</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>Out of that small group, a few are close friends I still talk to — now in frontend roles, a couple at names like <strong>Pickyourtrail</strong> and <strong>Eduseek AI</strong>.</li>
    <li>Their wins are their own; I'm just glad I was somewhere in the story. Their projects and words live on the <a href="https://thatpam.netlify.app/student-chapters" rel="noopener">student chapters <Icon name="external" class="doodle--thin" /></a> page.</li>
  </ul>

  <!--
    Adding media: drop files into public/images/work/thatpam/ and use one of these.

    <figure>
      <img src="/images/work/thatpam/landing.png" alt="Describe what the image shows" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Landing page, first cohort</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <video src="/images/work/thatpam/demo.mp4" poster="/images/work/thatpam/demo-poster.jpg" controls playsinline preload="none" width="1600" height="900"></video>
      <figcaption>Walkthrough of the cohort dashboard</figcaption>
    </figure>
  -->

  <h2>What stayed with me</h2>
  <ul class="doodle-list">
    <li>You don't need a slick, fully automated, self-serve product to start in education. Teaching runs on personal touch, taste and passion — that's what people feel, not your feature list.</li>
    <li>I made real money too (never the point), and at ~23 I got a close-up on the unglamorous parts: retention, and handling money young.</li>
  </ul>

  <blockquote>Cohorts are paused, but the learnings are permanent.</blockquote>
  <p>A pause, not a full stop — if someone reaches out tomorrow, I'd happily teach again under the same banner.</p>

  <aside class="callout wobbly wobbly--2" aria-label="Visit தட்பம்">
    <Icon name="pen" />
    <div>
      <strong>Read it in the wild</strong>
      <p>I wrote every word of this site myself back in 2021 — before LLMs were a thing. I was obsessed with copywriting and had a lot of fun with it. If you're comfortable in Tamil, give the copy a read and tell me what you think.</p>
      <p><a class="pill" href="https://thatpam.netlify.app/" rel="noopener">Visit thatpam.netlify.app <Icon name="external" /></a></p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</WorkLayout>
